From: Logos Maps <maps@logos.co>
Subject: [PATCH] OpenGL backend: forget the cached program when the context is shared

With Settings::SharedGLContext the core marks its cached GL state dirty
at the start of every frame (gl::Context::setDirtyState()), so that state
Qt changed between two map frames is re-applied. The program is the one
exception: DrawableGL::draw() compares the drawable's shader against the
cached *value* of the program state and only assigns -- and so only calls
glUseProgram -- when the value differs. The dirty flag is never consulted.
With the same drawables frame after frame the value never differs, and from
the second frame on every drawable was rendered with whatever program Qt
left current. Seen with a QQuickWindow texture node on Mesa/llvmpipe (Qt
6.9): the first frame after a style or tile change is right, every frame
after it is uniformly white (raster) or transparent (background), until
the next change creates a new program and the value differs again.

updateAssumedState() is the backend's hook for "the host used the context
since we last did"; it now also forgets the program (current value 0), so
the comparison in DrawableGL::draw() fails and the program is bound again.
The core-side fix would be a plain assignment there (State<> already
compares and honours the dirty flag); this keeps the change in the
binding.

---
diff --git a/src/core/CMakeLists.txt b/src/core/CMakeLists.txt
index d9a92a73..e5f732e4 100644
--- a/src/core/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/core/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -150,6 +150,8 @@ target_link_libraries(
     PRIVATE
         $<BUILD_INTERFACE:mbgl-compiler-options>
         $<BUILD_INTERFACE:mbgl-core>
+        # mbgl/gl/context.hpp (OpenGL renderer backend) needs the core's unique_resource header
+        $<BUILD_INTERFACE:mbgl-vendor-unique_resource>
         $<BUILD_INTERFACE:MLNQtCompilerOptions>
 )
 if(NOT MLN_QT_WITH_INTERNAL_SQLITE)
diff --git a/src/core/rendering/opengl_renderer_backend.cpp b/src/core/rendering/opengl_renderer_backend.cpp
index cbf523ed..2422c00b 100644
--- a/src/core/rendering/opengl_renderer_backend.cpp
+++ b/src/core/rendering/opengl_renderer_backend.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #include "opengl_renderer_backend_p.hpp"
 
 #include <mbgl/gfx/backend_scope.hpp>
+#include <mbgl/gl/context.hpp>
 #include <mbgl/gl/renderable_resource.hpp>
 
 #include <QtGlobal>
@@ -78,6 +79,18 @@ void OpenGLRendererBackend::deactivate() {
 void OpenGLRendererBackend::updateAssumedState() {
     assumeFramebufferBinding(ImplicitFramebufferBinding);
     assumeViewport(1, 1, size); // Use 1,1 to avoid zero-size viewport issues
+
+    // The context is shared with Qt (QOpenGLWidget / the Quick scene graph),
+    // which binds its own programs between two map frames. For a shared
+    // context the core marks its cached state dirty at the start of every
+    // frame, but DrawableGL::draw() compares the drawable's shader against
+    // the cached *value* of the program state and only assigns (and thus
+    // only calls glUseProgram) when the value differs -- the dirty flag is
+    // bypassed. With the same drawables frame after frame the value never
+    // differs, so from the second frame on everything was drawn with
+    // whatever program Qt left current (first frame right, then white or
+    // transparent). Forget the program: there is none we can assume.
+    getContext<mbgl::gl::Context>().program.setCurrentValue(0);
 }
 
 void OpenGLRendererBackend::restoreFramebufferBinding() {
